# Compiled binaries; `make build-*` targets output here (never commit build output)
stl-verify/dist/
# Loose Go binaries: `go build ./cmd/<group>/<name>` drops an executable named <name>
# in the working directory (stl-verify/ or the repo root). Build output belongs in
# stl-verify/dist/ (`make build-*`), never in the tree. One pattern per cmd/ entry,
# anchored to the two roots builds run from. Regenerate when cmd/ gains an entry:
#   ls -d stl-verify/cmd/*/*/ | xargs -n1 basename | sort -u
# Deliberately NOT listed: `internal` and `stress-test` — those names are also tracked
# directories at stl-verify/, and an ignore on the bare name would hide new files
# inside them. Build those two with -o dist/ (the Makefile targets already do).
/stl-verify/aave-like-user-snapshot-indexer
/aave-like-user-snapshot-indexer
/stl-verify/anchorage-indexer
/anchorage-indexer
/stl-verify/cex-orderbook-indexer
